KG42.register("clusters-9f9193788316ee79c1417407",{"id":"12-p2p_microgrid_trading::v142-d-K004","paper":"12-p2p_microgrid_trading","label":"Elecbay order fulfillment, deviation trading, and platform settlement","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K004","label":"Elecbay order fulfillment, deviation trading, and platform settlement","market_meaning":"Uses the committed quantities of accepted orders as the basis for fulfillment, connects fallback trading with the supplier and the corresponding monetary treatment when delivery deviations occur, and assigns billing, payment collection, and distribution responsibilities to Elecbay. The existing chains retain the procedural arrangements but do not yet constitute a complete computable settlement process.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M02"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["activation","settlement","coordination"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"Order acceptance, delivery deviations, and balancing contributions respectively condition the corresponding branches. Platform payment collection and settlement distribution belong to the same Elecbay process, but the scope of payment recipients, the determination of contributions, and pricing formulas remain to be clarified; the M03 simulation assumption of ignoring service fees is not adopted.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"Fulfillment and deviation handling share the same order commitment, and deviation trading has direct monetary consequences, thereby connecting execution and settlement. Order formation remains in v142-d-K003, and R008 is shared as a platform interface across stages.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R009","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides fulfillment responsibilities after order acceptance and supplier trading branches under delivery deviations."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R014","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Covers the monetary treatment of deviations, recording of balancing costs, and platform billing and payment distribution."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R008","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Shares the platform's order reception and payment collection interfaces; its primary assignment remains in v142-d-K003."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K004-L001","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","kind":"shared_node","from_refs":["v141-c-R008::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R008::V::bidding.supply"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R009::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R009::V::bidding.supply"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-13","v141-b-g01-ev-21"],"rationale":"The two chains reference the supply and demand submission entry points of the same platform. The shared nodes only identify the source of orders and cannot replace the order acceptance condition required by the R009 fulfillment branch."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K004-L002","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R014","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R014::phi::v141-c-R014-C001","v141-c-R014::phi::v141-c-R014-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-20","v141-b-g01-ev-26","v141-b-g01-ev-27"],"rationale":"The platform's receipt of payments connects to its billing, fee deduction, and distribution responsibilities; buyers' receipt of payments remains subject to the balancing contribution condition, and no monetary amount formula is generated on this basis."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K004-L003","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R014","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C005"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R014::phi::v141-c-R014-C003","v141-c-R014::phi::v141-c-R014-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-18","v141-b-g01-ev-19"],"rationale":"The same deviation from the committed quantity triggers fallback trading with the supplier and the corresponding price and penalty treatment. The execution activity and monetary treatment are complementary and are not treated as two independent deviation rules."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K004-L004","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R014","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C004"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R014::phi::v141-c-R014-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-17","v141-b-g01-ev-25"],"rationale":"Fulfillment activities during energy exchange connect to settlement records of the costs of balancing actions during the same period; the source supports an operational association, but the existing chains do not yet have a metered-quantity interface that can be mapped."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-O001","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R008::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R009::V::bidding.demand"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-21"],"rationale":"The same Elecbay demand submission function occurs in platform reception and in the steps preceding execution, with its different process uses retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-O002","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R008::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R009::V::bidding.supply"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-13","v141-b-g01-ev-21"],"rationale":"The same Elecbay supply submission function occurs in platform reception and in the steps preceding execution; this does not equate submission with acceptance."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-O003","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R008::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R014::V::coordination.local_operator"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-20","v141-b-g01-ev-26","v141-b-g01-ev-27"],"rationale":"The coordinator in both occurrences is the Elecbay platform, respectively showing the payment collection interface and the billing and distribution responsibilities; the platform is not equated with the DSO."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-O004","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R008::V::settlement.payment","v141-c-R014::V::settlement.payment"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-20","v141-b-g01-ev-27"],"rationale":"The two occurrences reference the payment function within the same platform process. R008-E003 and R014-E001 differ in direction and coverage and remain distinct frozen edges; no same_edge is registered."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G001","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"The existing C2 explanation for R009-C004 interprets the two precedence edges from bidding to execution as paths by which accepted orders enter execution, but the frozen edges record only precedence relationships and do not express network validation or acceptance status.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R009","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C004","v141-c-R009::E::v141-c-R009-E001","v141-c-R009::E::v141-c-R009-E002","v141-c-R008::V::coordination.local_operator"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-16","v141-b-g01-ev-17","v141-b-g01-ev-21","v141-b-g01-ev-22"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-prop-01"],"required_work":"Have the actual interface between order acceptance and execution clarified upstream, and review the C2 binding interpretation; for now, retain all frozen content without elevating a precedence relationship to an acceptance condition."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G002","category":"math_incomplete","description":"Supplier buying and selling prices, penalties, and service fees have only procedural references or references to external methods, lacking formal inputs, units, sign conventions, and calculation relationships. The specific conditions under which penalties apply are also not fully resolved. v141-b-g01-prop-02 remains pending.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R009","v141-c-R014"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C005","v141-c-R014::phi::v141-c-R014-C001","v141-c-R014::phi::v141-c-R014-C003","v141-c-R014::phi::v141-c-R014-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-18","v141-b-g01-ev-19","v141-b-g01-ev-27"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-prop-02"],"required_work":"Check the paper and the method referenced in its [23], and obtain the exact formulas, applicability conditions, and service fee definitions; establish computable settlement only after C clarifies the quantity roles, without independently adopting a general GB pricing formula."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G003","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"The payment recipients listed in ev20 include the DSO, and the scope modified by the balancing contribution qualification requires verification; the distribution descriptions in R014-C001 and ev27 are narrower, while R014-C002 retains only the buyer contribution branch. The existing chains do not fully resolve all payment recipients and their eligibility.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R008","v141-c-R014"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C003","v141-c-R014::phi::v141-c-R014-C001","v141-c-R014::phi::v141-c-R014-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-20","v141-b-g01-ev-27"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Verify the arrangements for payments to the DSO, the determination of balancing contributions, and the scope modified by the conditions; retain the frozen buyer branch without independently extending the conditions to other payment recipients or deleting DSO-related sources."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G004","category":"upstream_missing","description":"The sources mention metering of actual electricity generation and consumption and recording of balancing costs, but the frozen chains do not provide explicit data interfaces for committed quantities, actual quantities, and cost attribution; bill amounts cannot be inferred solely from process order.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R009","v141-c-R014"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C004","v141-c-R014::phi::v141-c-R014-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-17","v141-b-g01-ev-18","v141-b-g01-ev-25"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Obtain the metering time scope, the method for aligning committed and actual quantities, and the attribution of balancing costs, and then have C register the corresponding objects and relationships."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G005","category":"unverified_source","description":"The fulfillment, deviation handling, and settlement entries are all unaudited candidate sources; procedural connections do not constitute endorsement of source correctness or scientific closure.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R008","v141-c-R009","v141-c-R014"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-12","v141-b-g01-ev-13","v141-b-g01-ev-16","v141-b-g01-ev-17","v141-b-g01-ev-18","v141-b-g01-ev-19","v141-b-g01-ev-20","v141-b-g01-ev-21","v141-b-g01-ev-25","v141-b-g01-ev-26","v141-b-g01-ev-27","v141-b-g01-ev-28"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the cited original text, particularly the penalty wording, payment recipients, balancing contribution conditions, and the scope of applicability of the 1–31-day billing period."}]},"rule_refs":["12-p2p_microgrid_trading::v141-c-R009","12-p2p_microgrid_trading::v141-c-R014","12-p2p_microgrid_trading::v141-c-R008"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-3e8ef790cad9c018","COMP-739917e3869e45a6","COMP-b3f649e90c1f17b9","COMP-b9841ac99d9d29b8","KG31-f563e86a7a19f2a5"]});
